T*
(datasette #3046: Don't serve link: rel=next HTTP headers to Firefox for HTML pages I was) Tj
T*
(looking at the Firefox network panel today when I noticed that requests to a Datasette table) Tj
T*
(page were triggering an HTTP prefetch to the next page of rows in that table. This was) Tj
T*
(happening because Datasette pages serve an HTTP link header like this: link: ; rel="next" This) Tj
T*
(is bad. A tiny fraction of the visitors to one of those pages will click the "next" link, which) Tj
T*
(means their browser is fetching unnecessary data and the Datasette server is having to render) Tj
T*
(an entire page that then gets thrown away. I dug in and learned that Firefox has an issue that) Tj
T*
(has been open for 24 years about this behavior... And one of the early comments on that issue) Tj
T*
(links to my blog post from 2002 complaining about this feature. I hadn't just forgotten that I) Tj
T*
(had written about it, I had forgotten the feature entirely! Tags: firefox , html , mozilla ,) Tj
T*
(datasette) Tj
